 ],
 "title": "Linear Algebra, Theory and Applications",
 "byline": "Kenneth Kuttler \u00b7 Saylor Foundation / author\u2019s edition, September 2017 (CC BY)",
 "note": "PDF page = printed page. Exercise sections and the appendices (positive matrices, functions of matrices, ODEs, compactness, field extensions, selected answers) are not broken down. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "A thorough undergraduate-to-early-graduate linear algebra text that mixes matrix computation with theory and analysis. It starts from preliminaries (complex numbers, the fundamental theorem of algebra, division algorithm, F\u207f), covers matrices and linear maps, determinants with Cayley\u2013Hamilton, row operations and rank, LU and QR factorizations, eigenvalues with Schur\u2019s theorem and Gershgorin estimates, abstract vector spaces and fields, canonical forms (Jordan, rational), Markov chains, inner product spaces and least squares, self-adjoint operators with polar decomposition and SVD, norms and iterative methods, and numerical eigenvalue algorithms (power method, QR)."
}